    {
      "id": "webc3fl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to President"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The President is the head of the Indian State, the executive head of the Union, and the first citizen of India.",
        "Elected indirectly by an Electoral College consisting of elected members of both Houses of Parliament and State Legislative Assemblies.",
        "Qualifications require Indian citizenship, minimum 35 years of age, and eligibility for election as a member of the Lok Sabha.",
        "Impeachment procedure can be initiated in either House of Parliament only on the ground of 'violation of the Constitution' under Article 61.",
        "Exercises executive, legislative, financial, judicial, and emergency powers (Articles 352, 356, and 360) on the advice of the Union Council of Ministers."
      ],
      "id": "pi7qicv"
    },
